  "body": "**Wanted:** typed text in outline (TrueType or OpenType) fonts becomes closed shapes on the sketch entity. Those shapes can be pocketed, V-carved (#1443) or cut out. Typed single-stroke text is already placed by `insert_text` / #2679; this adds outline fonts. Signs and names are the most common hobby job. It needs font-outline parsing (glyph contours to lines and arcs or splines) and a clear refusal for a font that cannot be read.\n\n**Done means:** text in a chosen font produces closed shapes that pocket and cut out cleanly, through an undoable command and an MCP tool, pinned by tests.\n\nPart of #3066 (findings: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/3066#issuecomment-7050655107). The clean-room boundary of #3066 applies: no vendor wording, labels, parameter names or dialog flows.",
